Title = {Mineral alteration abnormity extraction from ETM data: Application in
   northwestern Yunnan, China},
Booktitle = {2008 PROCEEDINGS OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY AND ENVIRONMENTAL SYSTEM
   SCIENCES: ITESS 2008, VOL 4},
Year = {2008},
Pages = {408-412},
Abstract = {Mineral alteration abnormalities extractions based on ETM data have been
   made use in northwestern Yunnan, which belongs to Sanjiang area a famous
   mineralization belt China. Through the study on the spectral features of
   hydroxyl (OH) and iron ions (Fe2+ or Fe3+) related to mineral
   alterations, mineral alteration extraction methods are improved and a
   related process is developed. Interfering factors to mineral alterations
   are vegetation, snow and shadow. The vegetation is masked by ETM band
   ratio 5/4, while snow and shadow are masked by ETM band ratio 7/1. With
   these interefering factors masked, Principal Component Analysis (PCA) of
   ETM bands 1, 4, 5 and 7 is adopted for OH alterations extraction. PCA of
   ETM bands 1, 3, 4 and 5 are used for Fe2+ (Fe3+) alteration extraction.
   These alteration extractions are based on the principle that OH has high
   reflectance in band 5 and high absorption in band 3. Conversely, Fe2+
   (Fe3+) have high reflectance in band 3 and high absorption in bands 1, 4
   and 5. In addition, there is an uncertainty in alteration abnormity
   definition in the principal components (PCs), with a difficulty in
   classifying alteration abnormalities. To improve the shortcomings,
   alteration abnormity components were define by the contributions of
   their diagnostic spectral bands. While alteration abnormities are well
   classified by the standard deviation delta and average mu of abnormality
   component pixel value of normal distribution. Furthermore, analyses on
   alterations in study area are conducted in details along with geological
   survey and verification. Results show that the OH alteration is a main
   indicator of K feldspar, phyllic and prophilized alteration. These
   alterations are related to porphyry type copper deposit. The Fe2+ (Fe3+)
   alteration indicates pyritization, which is mainly related to
   hydrothermal or skarn type multi-mineral deposit. Drill holes are done
   in target areas, and new mining areas have been discovered by this way,
   the study reveals that the mineral alteration extraction process
   developed is practical in mineral exploration.},
Type = {Proceedings Paper},
Research-Areas = {Automation \& Control Systems; Computer Science; Environmental Sciences
   \& Ecology; Physical Geography; Remote Sensing; Telecommunications},
