Month = {DEC},
Abstract = {Underground environments present a challenge for hyperspectral outcrop
   analysis. In addition to operational safety and moisture, illumination
   is the main concern in data acquisition. We report a supercontinuum
   laser for illuminating rock faces in hyperspectral data acquisition. We
   present the early results of combining an off-the-shelf hyperspectral
   camera with a supercontinuum laser system, measured at night on rock
   faces in a former open-pit mine in southeast Spain as a proxy for
   underground lighting conditions. Band ratios specifically developed for
   this geological setting and low-light conditions highlight key minerals
   that can be used as a vector toward the ore zone. We successfully
   highlight the key indicator minerals and their distribution patterns for
   defining gold-bearing ore zones and that supercontinuum white laser
   light is a feasible illumination source for hyperspectral line scanners
   under field conditions.},
